Changes from the upstream project
---------------------------------

As required by section 2(a) of the LGPL-2.1, this section states which files
were changed and when. Changes were made by Joaquim Dalton-Pereira starting on
2026-10-13; the git history records each change and its date.

Derived from upstream and modified:

  - crates/scratchcad-occt-sys/
      Renamed from opencascade-sys. The files in src/ and include/, build.rs
      and OCCT/CMakeLists.txt come from upstream. C++ exceptions are now
      translated into Rust Results, null handles are checked, and bindings
      were added for more OpenCASCADE packages. Some files in include/ and
      OCCT/CMakeLists.txt are unchanged from upstream.
  - Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, rustfmt.toml, README.md
  - .github/workflows/

Copied from upstream unchanged: .clang-format, .gitignore and LICENSE.

New in this project:

  - crates/scratchcad-occt-rhai/ (the Rhai scripting API and occt-rhai tool)
  - crates/scratchcad-occt-sys/README.md and crates/scratchcad-occt-sys/tests/
  - docs/rhai-api.md
  - .github/actions/ and .github/dependabot.yml
  - Any file under crates/scratchcad-occt-sys/src/ or include/ that has no
    counterpart in upstream opencascade-sys

Removed from upstream: the opencascade, occt-sys, model-api, viewer,
kicad-parser and wasm-example crates, the examples, CHANGELOG.md and the
upstream docs.


Third-party software
--------------------

This repository does not include source code from the following projects. They
are downloaded by Cargo at build time and each one carries its own license.

  - OpenCASCADE Technology (https://dev.opencascade.org)
      LGPL-2.1 with the Open CASCADE Exception. Built from source by the
      occt-sys crate when the `builtin` feature is enabled, or linked from a
      system installation.
  - Rust crates listed in Cargo.lock, such as cxx, rhai, glam and thiserror,
    which are mostly licensed under MIT and/or Apache-2.0.

Binaries built from this project include OpenCASCADE and these crates, so
anyone who distributes such a binary must also include their license texts.
